    "description": "Educational Resource\nGeological Mineral Set & Jamestown, Virginia Mineral Specimens\nNatural Geological Specimens in Original Packaging\n10\" x 7\" x 3\"\nOriginal Multi-Piece Sets\nThis collection includes two vintage educational mineral sets designed for the study of earth science. The primary \"Geological Mineral Set\" features 24 mounted specimens including unique items such as Dinosaur Bone, Petrified Wood, and Sulphur, each labeled with its classification and geographic origin. Accompanied by the \"Jamestown, Virginia\" set containing 12 specimens, this lot provides a comprehensive overview of common and rare minerals found throughout North America, including Obsidian, Rose Quartz, and Zinc Ore.\nIncludes 24-specimen Earth Science set and 12-specimen Jamestown collection\nOriginal yellow \"Guide to Rocks & Minerals\" instructional booklet included\nSpecimens are securely mounted to identification cards with original vintage typography\nCombined dimensions approximately 10\" x 7\" x 3\" for the two boxes\nCondition:\nGood vintage condition. The specimens are largely intact and well-preserved on their original mounting cards. The outer boxes show age-appropriate wear, including some toning, minor staining to the teal lid, and edge rubbing typical of educational materials from the mid-20th century. The interior cards show light foxing, but all text remains clear and legible.\nPlease Note:\nThis is a pre-owned item being sold\nas-is\n. We do our best to describe items accurately and include research where possible, but we are not experts in every category. Please note that if the title or description states \"Tested\" that we only test to make sure the unit \"\nPOWERS ON\"\n.\nNo further testing takes place unless stated otherwise and items are considered untested.\nPlease remember all items are used and are sold as is, no refunds.If you have questions, please contact us before bidding.\nFor all vintage clothing, please research sizing before 